A||||8||theogre||easier headlight changing||||1
Z||000000||theogre||10-23-1999||03:33 PM||||If you've ever seen the "recomended" procedure for changing headlight bulbs, or worse tried to follow it, then I have some good news for you.<P>There is an easier way and you only have to open the hood once!<P>Open the hood and turn on the head lights. Now unplug the motors and the lamps. turn the headlight switch off to sve the battery.<P>Next disconnect the lif link from the bottom of the headlight frame. You need a T30 torx bit and a 10mm wrench.<P>Now you can flip the whole frame up to work on it. You'll need to spring the hood a smidge to get by the edge, then lift the door to clear the hinge.<P>All the rest of the trim and clamp are now easy to work on.<P>This method took me about half the time as trying the "recomended" method in the various books.<P>When your finished shoot everything with a bit of spray oil. WD40, Duralube, what ever you favorite is. Don't grease the pivots. Grease holds lots of dirt.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ka4nkf||10-23-1999||03:58 PM||||This Sounds Great. The Factory Way Stinks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||10-23-1999||04:24 PM||||Ogre, thanks again I was going to buy those super blue bulbs today and try to install them. Grand Auto has them. Someone on this fourm posted this a while back, but just like I said in one of my post I just seem to wait and you will post what I need||||reg||10
